<p class="govuk-body">The court decided you had to spend time in prison. This is called being in custody.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">You have been released from prison into the community. This is called being on licence.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">While you are on licence, you must follow your licence conditions and keep in touch with your probation officer.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">Some people on probation move to a stage where they don’t need to go to in-person appointments when they are in the community. This does not apply to everyone. Your probation officer will tell you if this applies to you.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">If you are eligible for this, your probation meetings will stop. You must still follow the rules of your licence. You can still speak to your probation officer to access support, if you need it.</p>
